# Netlify redirects — Loisirs 73
#
# Every path here is one the site's own footer links. The chrome writes clean
# URLs (/cgv, /signaler, /de/mentions-legales); the files on disk carry .html
# and, for the two regulated pages, a phase marker. These rules join the two.
# gate_link_integrity reads this file, so a footer link with no page and no
# rule turns the build red rather than shipping a 404.
#
# Status 200 = rewrite (the clean URL stays in the address bar).
# Status 301 = redirect (legacy or alias paths that should collapse).

# --- Regulated pages (French law, published once, in French) ------------------
# Mentions légales and the privacy policy are the publisher's statements under
# the LCEN and the RGPD. They exist in French only and every locale points at
# the same document — translating a legal statement would create a second text
# that could disagree with the first.
